{"unit":"review","questions":[{"q":"Which statement about triangles is TRUE?","options":["The interior angles of an equilateral triangle are equal","All sides of an isosceles triangle are equal","The interior angles of an obtuse triangle are all obtuse","A right triangle has 2 right angles"],"why":"An equilateral triangle has 3 equal angles (60° each). An isosceles triangle has only 2 equal sides.","src":"Unit 7: Review Q1, p.245","fig":null},{"q":"ABC is an equilateral triangle and BC = 10 cm. How long is AB?","options":["10 cm","5 cm","20 cm","30 cm"],"why":"All 3 sides of an equilateral triangle are equal, so AB = BC = 10 cm.","src":"Unit 7: Review Q2(a), p.245","fig":{"w":320,"h":230,"pts":{"A":[150,30],"B":[250,200],"C":[50,200]},"items":[{"t":"poly","p":["A","B","C"],"fill":"#FFE0B2"},{"t":"tick","p":["A","B"]},{"t":"tick","p":["B","C"]},{"t":"tick","p":["A","C"]},{"t":"ang","v":"C","a":"A","b":"B","s":"60°"},{"t":"len","p":["B","C"],"s":"10 cm"},{"t":"pl","p":"A","d":[0.0,-11.0]},{"t":"pl","p":"B","d":[15.7,15.9]},{"t":"pl","p":"C","d":[-15.7,15.9]}]}},{"q":"An isosceles triangle has a vertex angle of 70°. What is each of the other 2 angles?","options":["55°","110°","70°","35°"],"why":"180° - 70° = 110°. Share it between 2 equal angles: 110° ÷ 2 = 55°.","src":"Unit 7: Review Q3(b), p.246","fig":null},{"q":"ABC is a triangle with ∠ACB = 90° and AC = CB = 5 cm. What type of triangle is it?","options":["A right isosceles triangle","An equilateral triangle","An obtuse triangle","A scalene triangle"],"why":"It has a right angle AND 2 equal sides, so it is right and isosceles.","src":"Unit 7: Review Q4(a), p.246","fig":null},{"q":"A straight line joining any two points on the circumference is called a…","options":["Chord","Radius","Center","Circumference"],"why":"Any line joining 2 points on the edge is a chord. A diameter is the longest chord.","src":"Unit 7: Review Q5, p.247","fig":null},{"q":"Which solid is this?","options":["Pyramid","Prism","Cone","Cuboid"],"why":"It has a flat base and triangle faces that meet at a vertex.","src":"Unit 8: Review Q8(a), p.248","fig":{"w":320,"h":230,"pts":{},"items":[{"t":"poly","p":[[70.0,200],[230.0,200],[165,30]],"fill":"#C8E6C9"},{"t":"poly","p":[[230.0,200],[270.0,165],[165,30]],"fill":"#C8E6C9"},{"t":"seg","p":[[270.0,165],[110.0,165]],"dash":true,"width":1.5},{"t":"seg","p":[[110.0,165],[70.0,200]],"dash":true,"width":1.5},{"t":"seg","p":[[110.0,165],[165,30]],"dash":true,"width":1.5},{"t":"seg","p":[[70.0,200],[165,30]]},{"t":"seg","p":[[230.0,200],[165,30]]},{"t":"seg","p":[[270.0,165],[165,30]]}]}},{"q":"Which solid is this?","options":["Cone","Cylinder","Pyramid","Sphere"],"why":"1 circle face, 1 curved face and 1 vertex.","src":"Unit 8: Review Q8(b), p.248","fig":{"w":320,"h":230,"pts":{},"items":[{"t":"poly","p":[[90,180],[160,30],[230,180]],"fill":"#D1C4E9"},{"t":"ell","c":[160,180],"rx":70,"ry":20,"half":"front","fill":"#D1C4E9"},{"t":"ell","c":[160,180],"rx":70,"ry":20,"half":"back","dash":true}]}},{"q":"Which solid is this?","options":["Cylinder","Cone","Prism","Sphere"],"why":"2 circle faces and 1 curved face.","src":"Unit 8: Review Q8(c), p.248","fig":{"w":320,"h":230,"pts":{},"items":[{"t":"poly","p":[[95,45],[225,45],[225,185],[95,185]],"fill":"#FFE0B2"},{"t":"ell","c":[160,185],"rx":65,"ry":18,"fill":"#FFE0B2"},{"t":"poly","p":[[95,45],[225,45],[225,185],[95,185]],"fill":"#FFE0B2"},{"t":"ell","c":[160,185],"rx":65,"ry":18,"half":"front"},{"t":"ell","c":[160,185],"rx":65,"ry":18,"half":"back","dash":true},{"t":"ell","c":[160,45],"rx":65,"ry":18,"fill":"#FFE0B2"}]}},{"q":"Which solid is this?","options":["Pyramid","Prism","Cone","Cube"],"why":"Triangle faces meet at a vertex on a triangle base.","src":"Unit 8: Review Q8(d), p.248","fig":{"w":320,"h":230,"pts":{},"items":[{"t":"poly","p":[[60.0,190],[260.0,190],[160,20]],"fill":"#C8E6C9"},{"t":"seg","p":[[260.0,190],[170,160]],"dash":true,"width":1.5},{"t":"seg","p":[[170,160],[60.0,190]],"dash":true,"width":1.5},{"t":