C":[290,170],"_H":[86,45]},"items":[{"t":"poly","p":["_A","_B","_C"],"fill":"#FFE0B2"},{"t":"len","p":["_A","_B"],"s":"9 cm"},{"t":"len","p":["_B","_C"],"s":"22 cm"},{"t":"len","p":["_C","_A"],"s":"20 cm"},{"t":"seg","p":["_A",[62,30]],"dash":true},{"t":"seg","p":[[62,30],"_B"],"dash":true},{"t":"txt","at":[45,80],"s":"8 cm","size":15,"bold":true,"color":"#1565c0"}]}},{"q":"Find the perimeter of the triangle.","options":["54 cm","56 cm","99 cm","48 cm"],"why":"Add the 3 sides: 23 + 20 + 11 = 54 cm.","src":"Unit 9: Review Q10(d), p.250","fig":{"w":320,"h":230,"pts":{"_A":[40,170],"_B":[150,170],"_C":[280,40],"_P":[280,170]},"items":[{"t":"poly","p":["_A","_B","_C"],"fill":"#D1C4E9"},{"t":"seg","p":["_B","_P"],"dash":true},{"t":"seg","p":["_P","_C"],"dash":true},{"t":"ra","v":"_P","a":"_C","b":"_B"},{"t":"len","p":["_A","_B"],"s":"11 cm","off":16},{"t":"len","p":["_A","_C"],"s":"23 cm","off":-16},{"t":"len","p":["_B","_C"],"s":"20 cm","off":16},{"t":"len","p":["_P","_C"],"s":"18 cm","off":-18}]}},{"q":"Each square is 1 cm. Find the area of the shaded triangle.","options":["8.5 cm²","11.5 cm²","20 cm²","10 cm²"],"why":"Rectangle 5 × 4 = 20 cm². White triangles: 6 + 3 + 2.5 = 11.5 cm². 20 - 11.5 = 8.5 cm².","src":"Unit 9: Review Q11, p.250","fig":{"w":170,"h":144,"pts":{"_P":[20,124],"_Q":[98,20],"_R":[150,98]},"items":[{"t":"grid","x":20,"y":20,"cols":5,"rows":4,"size":26},{"t":"poly","p":["_P","_Q","_R"],"fill":"#BBDEFB"}]}},{"q":"Each interior angle of hexagon ABCDEF is 120°. What is the sum of its interior angles?","options":["720°","540°","360°","600°"],"why":"120° × 6 = 720°. (A hexagon's angles always add up to 720°.)","src":"Unit 10: Review Q16(a), p.253","fig":{"w":320,"h":230,"pts":{"_0":[115.0,42.1],"_1":[205.0,42.1],"_2":[250.0,120.0],"_3":[205.0,197.9],"_4":[115.0,197.9],"_5":[70.0,120.0]},"items":[{"t":"poly","p":["_0","_1","_2","_3","_4","_5"],"fill":"#BBDEFB"},{"t":"ang","v":"_0","a":"_5","b":"_1","s":"120°","r":20}]}},{"q":"Pentagon IJKLM is a triangle (84°, 48°, 48°) on top of a rectangle. What is the sum of its interior angles?","options":["540°","360°","720°","180°"],"why":"(84° + 48° + 48°) + (90° × 4) = 180° + 360° = 540°.","src":"Unit 10: Review Q16(b), p.253","fig":{"w":320,"h":230,"pts":{"I":[160,20],"J":[240,90],"K":[240,200],"L":[80,200],"M":[80,90]},"items":[{"t":"poly","p":["I","J","K","L","M"],"fill":"#C8E6C9"},{"t":"seg","p":["M","J"],"dash":true},{"t":"ang","v":"I","a":"M","b":"J","s":"84°","r":20},{"t":"ang","v":"M","a":"I","b":"J","s":"48°","r":26},{"t":"ra","v":"K","a":"J","b":"L"},{"t":"ra","v":"L","a":"K","b":"M"},{"t":"pl","p":"I","d":[0.0,-9.0]},{"t":"pl","p":"J","d":[15.0,1.4]},{"t":"pl","p":"K","d":[11.3,18.3]},{"t":"pl","p":"L","d":[-11.3,18.3]},{"t":"pl","p":"M","d":[-15.0,1.4]}]}},{"q":"A figure is a 15 cm square with a triangle of sides 16.2 cm attached. Its outside edges are 15, 16.2, 16.2, 15, 15 and 15 cm. Perimeter?","options":["92.4 cm","76.2 cm","108.6 cm","92 cm"],"why":"15 + 16.2 + 16.2 + 15 + 15 + 15 = 92.4 cm.","src":"Unit 10: Review Q17(a), p.253","fig":null},{"q":"A polygon has sides of 18 cm, 16 cm, 18 cm and six sides of 7 cm. Perimeter?","options":["94 cm","59 cm","87 cm","101 cm"],"why":"18 + 16 + 18 = 52, and 6 × 7 = 42. 52 + 42 = 94 cm.","src":"Unit 10: Review Q17(b), p.253","fig":null},{"q":"A figure is made of a 7 cm square and an 11 cm square. What is its area?","options":["170 cm²","77 cm²","36 cm²","324 cm²"],"why":"7 × 7 = 49 and 11 × 11 = 121. 49 + 121 = 170 cm².","src":"Unit 10: Review Q18(a), p.254","fig":null},{"q":"O is the center. Find the circumference of the circle. Leave the answer in terms of π.","options":["16π cm","8π cm","64π cm","32π cm"],"why":"Circumference = 2 × π × radius = 2 × π × 8 = 16π cm.","src":"Unit 11: Review Q20(a), p.256","fig":{"w":320,"h":240,"pts":{"O":[160,120]},"items":[{"t":"circle","c":[160,120],"r":90,"fill":"#FFE0B2"},{"t":"dot","p":[160,120]},{"t":"seg","p":[[160,120],[250,120]]},{"t":"len","p":[[160,120],[250,120]],"s":"8 cm","off":-14},{"t":"pl","p":"O","d":[-12,20]}]}},{"q":"O is the center. Find the circumference of the circle. Leave the answer in terms of π.","options":["31π cm","62π cm","15.5π cm","961π cm"],"why":"Circumference = π × diameter = π × 31 = 31π cm.","src":"Unit 11: Review Q20(c), p.256","fig":{"w":320,"h":240,"pts":{"O":[160,120]},"items":[{"t":"circle","c":[160,120],"r":90,"fill":"#FFE0B2"},{"t":"dot","p":[160,120]},{"t":"seg","p":[[70,120],[250,120]]},{"t":"len","p":[[70,120],[250,120]],"s":"31 cm","off":-14},{"t":"pl","p":"O","d":[-12,20]}]}},{"q":"Radius 42 cm. Find the circumference. (Take π ≈ 22/7.)","options":["264 cm","132 cm","5,544 cm","528 cm"],"why":"2 × 22/7 × 42: 84 ÷ 7 = 12, 22 × 12 = 264 cm.","src":"Unit 11: Review Q21(a), p.257","fig":{"w":320,"h":240,"pts":{"O":[160,120]},"items":[{"t":"circle","c":[160,120],"r":90,"fill":"#BBDEFB"},{"t":"dot","p":[160,120]},{"t":"seg","p":[[160,120],[250,120]]},{"t":"len","p":[[160,120],[250,120]],"s":"42 cm","off":-14},{"t":"pl","p":"O","d":[-12,20]}]}},{"q":"Radius 6 m. Find the area. (Take π ≈ 3.14.)","options":["113.04 m²","37.68 m²","18.84 m²","452.16 m²"],"why":"3.14 × 6 × 6 = 3.14 × 36 = 113.04 m².","src":"Unit 11: Review Q22(a), p.257","fig":{"w":320,"h":240,"pts":{"O":[160,120]},"items":[{"t":"circle","c":[160,120],"r":90,"fill":"#FFF59D"},{"t":"dot","p":[160,120]},{"t":"seg","p":[[160,120],[250,120]]},{"t":"len","p":[[160,120],[250,120]],"s":"6 m","off":-14},{"t":"pl","p":"O","d":[-12,20]}]}},{"q":"An acrylic sheet is 2 quarter circles (radius 5 cm) and a 12 cm by 5 cm rectangle. Perimeter? (Take π ≈ 3.14.)","options":["49.7 cm","39.7 cm","31.4 cm","44.7 cm"],"why":"The 2 quarter arcs make half a circle: ½ × 2 × 3.14 × 5 = 15.7 cm. Then 15.7 + 12 + 12 + 5 + 5 = 49.7 cm.","src":"Unit 11: Review Q23, p.258","fig":null},{"q":"An L-shaped solid is 6 cm deep. Its front is a 27 cm × 6 cm base with a 15 cm × 18 cm column on top. Volume?","options":["2,592 cm³","432 cm³","1,620 cm³","2,952 cm³"],"why":"Front area = 27 × 6 + 15 × 18 = 162 + 270 = 432 cm². Volume = 432 × 6 = 2,592 cm³.","src":"Unit 12: Review Q25(c), p.259","fig":null},{"q":"A step solid: a 30 × 24 × 11 block with a 30 × 12 × 11 block on top (cm). Volume?","options":["11,880 cm³","7,920 cm³","3,960 cm³","15,840 cm³"],"why":"30 × 24 × 11 = 7,920 and 30 × 12 × 11 = 3,960. 7,920 + 3,960 = 11,880 cm³.","src":"Unit 12: Review Q25(d), p.259","fig":null},{"q":"A 12 m × 18 m × 30 m block has an 8 m × 14 m hole all the way down. Volume?","options":["3,120 m³","6,480 m³","3,360 m³","9,840 m³"],"why":"12 × 18 × 30 = 6,480. Hole: 8 × 14 × 30 = 3,360. 6,480 - 3,360 = 3,120 m³.","src":"Unit 12: Review Q25(e), p.259","fig":null},{"q":"Tank A (30 × 10 × 20 cm) is full. Tank B (50 × 12 × 30 cm) is ¼ full. All of A is poured into B. New volume in B?","options":["10,500 cm³","6,000 cm³","4,500 cm³","18,000 cm³"],"why":"A = 30 × 10 × 20 = 6,000 cm³. B had ¼ × 50 × 12 × 30 = 4,500 cm³. 6,000 + 4,500 = 10,500 cm³.","src":"Unit 12: Review Q26(a), p.260","fig":null},{"q":"Tank B (base 50 cm × 12 cm) now holds 10,500 cm³. Water height?","options":["17.5 cm","175 cm","21 cm","7.5 cm"],"why":"10,500 ÷ (50 × 12) = 10,500 ÷ 600 = 17.5 cm.","src":"Unit 12: Review Q26(b), p.260","fig":null},{"q":"5, 14, 23, 32, 41, … What is term 62?","options":["554","563","558","549"],"why":"The jump is 9. Term 62 has 61 jumps: 5 + (61 × 9) = 5 + 549 = 554.","src":"Unit 13: Review Q27, p.261","fig":null},{"q":"5, 14, 23, 32, 41, … What is the rule?","options":["Add 9 each time","Add 5 each time","Add 7 each time","Multiply by 3"],"why":"14 - 5 = 9, 23 - 14 = 9. The pattern adds 9 each time.","src":"Unit 13: Review Q27, p.261","fig":null},{"q":"1 triangle needs 3 toothpicks, 2 need 6, 3 need 9. How many toothpicks for 28 triangles?","options":["84","81","31","56"],"why":"Each triangle needs 3 toothpicks: 28 × 3 = 84.","src":"Unit 13: Review Q28, p.261","fig":null},{"q":"Separate toothpick triangles: 3, 6, 9, 12, … How many toothpicks for 10 triangles?","o